# Credit Card Fraud Detection System

## About the Project
This project uses Python and machine learning to classify credit card transactions as potentially fraudulent or normal.

## Technologies Used
- Python
- Pandas and NumPy
- Matplotlib and Seaborn
- Scikit-learn
- Google Colab

## Machine Learning Algorithms
- Decision Tree Classifier
- K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)

## Features
- Data analysis and visualization
- Model training and prediction
- Confusion matrix and classification report
- Interactive transaction-prediction interface

## How to Run
1. Download the `.ipynb` notebook.
2. Open [Google Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/).
3. Upload the notebook and run the cells.
4. Upload the required dataset when prompted.

## Note
This is an educational project. The model's fraud-detection performance is limited and requires further improvement before real-world use.
